{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who devises to do evil, him they call a schemer</b> — [verses] 8–9, two joined [verses]. That is, one who devises evil — the readers will call him \"master of schemes,\" like the matter: \"and he called to him El, the Elohim of Israel.\" And the meaning: they will call his name and it will be so called, because the scheming of a man is folly, and his thought is to commit sin, and this is \"the scheming of folly is sin.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:27.976971720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}